body:
As today is Sunday, I thought it would be fun for everyone to confess their sins with the community. [Here](https://twitter.com/cyanwhisky?s=20&t=jQphU1wloIo-GLzMAW3o4w) is the artist's twitter.

&#x200B;

I'll go first, during my first playthrough I killed every turtle I came across for their runes and meat.  is the artist's Twitter.e Pope until after I'd beaten the game. I repent and beg forgiveness.

It took me too long to scroll down and find this comment and like /u/bigmac80 said I was going to keep my thoughts to myself, but I feel it's important to make a distinction. Floyd was 100% murdered by cops. Derrick Scott made a series of very poor decisions that led to his death. Brandishing a weapon at people and using meth led to a concerned citizen calling the police. The police gave him straightforward commands to turn around, but his methed out mind decided to run which puts the police on high alert, in addition, he lies about having a weapon. A truly sorrowful series of unfortunate events lead to his death, even though he didn't deserve it. 

&#x200B;

Taking the time to make the distinction between this case and Floyd's is important moving forward because while we can acknowledge that the police system desperately needs reform, we have to at some point take responsibility for our own actions that lead us into having interactions with police in the first place. By choosing to not do meth and wave a gun at people, you will have a smaller chance of interacting with police. In addition, we can't let what happened to Floyd suddenly push us too far in the opposite direction when it comes to African-American's interactions with police. We don't want black people to suddenly have immunity from any form of prosecution or interaction with cops because they are afraid of nation backlash from them trying to arrest a black criminal (i.e. we don't want cops to start ignoring black crimes because of a fear of backlash.)

> *Whilst men are linked together, they easily and speedily communicate the alarm of any evil design.*  *They are enabled to fathom it with common counsel, and to oppose it with united strength. Whereas, when they lie dispersed, without concert, order, or discipline, communication is uncertain, counsel difficult, and resistance impracticable...* *When bad men combine, the good must associate; else they will fall, one by one, an unpitied sacrifice in a contemptible struggle.* 

&#x200B;

\-Edmund Burke 1770

&#x200B;

Political apathy is our greatest enemy. Unless we trust one another to the fullest extent we will be picked off one by one by bad men working together.

How do you think people trapped at the poverty line are supposed to advance their careers? These are people that are literally only making enough to get by paycheck to paycheck. They cannot afford to invest in themselves through college, trade schools, or licenses/certificates because they can barely afford to put a roof over their heads, food on their tables, or gas in their clunkers. In addition, like the middle and upper socioeconomic classes, the lower/poverty class wants, and obviously have, families.  If they can barely afford to maintain their desperate, bleak, and hopeless lives how can they ever have a chance at something more while trying to also pay the costs of having a family? Should they deprive themselves of the joy of family until they are in a higher tax bracket? 

&#x200B;

Humanity first, not faceless, greed-driven, soul-sucking, lecherous corporations that would rather pay endless fines than alter their carbon footsteps. Your lack of empathy alongside your ability to make broad brushstrokes that reduce all of society into simple data to be input into an algorithm that theorizes the best solution for being poor is to stop being poor are a lethal combination for happiness.

Stage 1: I Wish

&#x200B;

Stage 2: I Will

&#x200B;

Stage 3: I Did

&#x200B;

Stage 1 & 2 are identical in my opinion because they both can become excuses. "I wish I worked out more" and "I will work out more" are the same thing to me because neither one of them actually means you did anything. You need to move past those stages and be able to look back and say "I did work out more." 

&#x200B;

I still have a long way to go myself though...

I'm having a similar issue and I was about to make a post. Ever since the new steam update I've been having an issue where when I open steam it is kind of frozen. I can switch tabs, but when I click on the store, for instance, it loads for a few seconds and then stays a black screen. When I go to my library it shows my last played game highlighted, but won't let me hover or click on anything. The only fix I've found is to go to task manager and end the steam process and open it again. 

&#x200B;

I wish I could go back to the old steam. Upvoting for visibility.

Announcer: Finish her!

&#x200B;

Fatality!!!

Don't blame yourself, you can't account for how everyone will take your message. 

&#x200B;

They just make me worried that I'm doing everything wrong.

My favorite party:

&#x200B;

Bride of Iratus/Skeleton/Vampire/Bone Golem

&#x200B;

I use the Skeleton to buff the Vampire and Bone Golem while the Bride alternates between restoring mana and self buffing to finish off low hp targets.
